WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.740
- [Instructor] Let's see if we can compute

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:06.740
what 1.86 divided by two is.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.610
And like always pause this
video and have a go at it.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.700
And I'll give you a hint,
see if you can think

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:17.380
about 1.86 as a certain
number of hundredths,

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.903
and then divide that by two.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.340
All right now let's work
through it together.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.320
So as promised, let's see if we can

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.950
think of 1.86 as a certain
number of hundredths.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.700
So if we go to the hundredths place,

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.880
we only see six there, but we could

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.680
view 8/10 as 80 hundredths.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.350
So you could view the
.86 as 86 hundredths,

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:44.170
and each one is 100
hundredths, so we really

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.520
have 186 hundredths.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.630
So this number right over here I'm going

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:54.630
to rewrite as 186 hundredths, hundredths.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.420
And that is what we need to divide by two.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.320
Now, if you're dividing
186 of something by two,

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.670
well it's just gonna be 186 divided by two

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:09.800
of that something.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:14.800
So we could rewrite this
as 186 divided by two,

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.340
and then that's the number of hundredths

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.600
this is going to be, so I'll
put that in parenthesis.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.453
So it's going to be that
many hundredths, hundredths.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:31.380
All right, so what is 186 divided by two?

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.070
Some of you might be able
to do it in your head,

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:36.660
some of you might wanna use some paper.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:40.130
The way I like to think
about it is if I were to take

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:43.760
the six ones and divide it by two,

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.800
well that's going to be three ones.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:50.180
And then if I were to take the 18 tens

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:53.830
and divided by two, that's
going to be nine tens,

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:56.120
so that gets us to 93.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.710
Now you could've also
thought about it like this,

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.680
you could've said, how many times does two

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.680
go into 186?

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.240
Let's see, it doesn't go into one,

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.870
how many times does it go into 18?

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:08.750
Nine times, nine times two is 18,

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.970
we could subtract, and then you have zero,

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.430
you bring down that six.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:16.870
Two goes into six three
times, three times two is six.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.530
You subtract and you get no remainders.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.550
So either way you're going to get 93.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.280
And it's 93 what?

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.860
Well it's 93 hundredths, is
what we're talking about.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.850
93 hundredths.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:32.030
And now we just wanna
express 93 hundredths

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.340
as a decimal.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.740
Well how do we do that?

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.532
Well that's gonna be 0 point.

00:02:36.532 --> 00:02:41.532
The 90 hundredths is
the same thing as 9/10,

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:46.000
and then the three hundredths,
is of course 300 hundredths.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.010
Three in the hundredths place.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:50.680
So it's 0.93, and so we
can write it up here.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:54.140
This is going to be equal to 0.93,

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.163
and we're done!

